---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import CookieBanner from '../components/CookieBanner.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '22 October 2026';
---

<Base title="Privacy — Duskfleet" description="What the Duskfleet website collects, and how to change your cookie choice.">
  <Header />
  <main>
    <article class="privacy">
      <div class="container privacy__inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="h2">What this website collects</h1>
        <p class="lead">Last updated {updated}.</p>

        <section>
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <p>
            duskfleet.com is a static page with no accounts, no forms and no tracking by default.
            The only optional data collection is Google Analytics, and it runs only after you choose
            <strong>Accept</strong> in the cookie banner. The Duskfleet software itself runs on your own
            machine and never talks to this website.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Hosting</h2>
          <p>
            The site is served by GitHub Pages. Like any web host, GitHub may record your IP address in
            server logs to keep the service running. See the
            <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Analytics, only with your consent</h2>
          <p>
            If you accept, we load Google Analytics 4 to learn how many people visit, which pages they
            read and where they come from. It sets the <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> cookies
            (kept for up to two years) and sends page views, scrolls and outbound clicks to Google.
            GA4 does not log or store IP addresses; they are used only to derive coarse location and then
            discarded. Advertising storage and personalisation stay off. Event data is kept for 14 months.
            Google processes this data on our behalf; see
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Besides those, the site sends a few events of its own, so we can tell which links and answers
            are useful. Every value comes from a fixed list in the site's code: no free text, no addresses,
            nothing about you.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>click_install_cta</code>: an Install button was clicked (hero or navigation).</li>
            <li>
              <code>click_github</code>: a link to GitHub was clicked, with where it sits on the page and
              whether it leads to the repository, the releases or the license.
            </li>
            <li>
              <code>click_docs</code>: a documentation link was clicked, with where it sits and which
              document it opens.
            </li>
            <li><code>faq_open</code>: an FAQ answer was opened, with a short id of the question.</li>
            <li><code>view_section</code>: a section of the home page came into view, once per visit.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Nothing loads before you choose Accept. If you reject, or make no choice, nothing is loaded,
            no event is sent and no analytics cookie is set.
          </p>
          <p>
            <button type="button" id="change-consent" class="btn btn--ghost">Change your cookie choice</button>
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Nothing else</h2>
          <p>
            We do not collect names, emails or any other personal data on this site. Links to GitHub,
            documentation and releases take you to github.com, which has its own privacy terms.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Questions</h2>
          <p>
            Open an issue on the <a href={site.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Duskfleet repository</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
  <CookieBanner />
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  document.getElementById('change-consent')?.addEventListener('click', function () {
    try { localStorage.removeItem('duskfleet-consent'); } catch (e) {}
    location.reload();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: var(--section-pad) calc(var(--section-pad) + 80px);
  }

  .privacy__inner {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .privacy section {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    line-height: 28px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .privacy p {
    margin-top: 12px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 26px;
  }

  .privacy ul {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 26px;
  }

  .privacy strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .privacy code {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .privacy a:not(.btn) {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-position: from-font;
  }

  .privacy .btn {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
</style>
